      "writtenOn": "2020-10-13T20:19:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it does indeed mean that.\n\nBazel currently does not have an API with the capability to report the files that it actually read -- neither from globs, nor BUILD/bzl/workspace files.\nThis is certainly not ideal for partial analysis in mixed-builds. That said, as it currently stands, soong needs to re-evaluate the entire tree anyway, so each build will almost certainly use each BUILD/bzl/WORKSPACE in the entire source tree, anyway. (Unless they\u0027re effectively dead code!)\n\nThanks for asking, it\u0027s reminded me that we should track this. I\u0027ve filed b/170756504.",
      "parentUuid": "938c59a8_52b9b163",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "800cd4cd10872a900aee358100db2d1bf7cba7f6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
